  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 114 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nThe mid-west low will move east across KY early next week which \nallows the ridge to build east across the central and southern \nplains once again. This will lead to increasing highs once again \nwith widespread 100s forecast by Monday. Currently Monday has the \nhighest probability of 100+ degree temperatures for the entire week \nat around 50 percent in the east and west Panhandles, but over 90 \npercent for north-central and SE areas per the NBM. Ridge roller \nS/WV disturbances will encounter a decent monsoon moisture axis next \nweek leading to chances for storms despite the hot temperatures. NBM \nshows slight chances for rain assoc with this activity Tue and Wed \nevenings favoring the NW Panhandles. POPs are only around 10 percent \nby Thursday, but models are diverging by end of the week regarding \nthe strength of the ridge and a possible weakness developing over \nthe Panhandles (per the last few GFS operational runs). If this were \nto occur, we can expect better rain chances and slightly lower \ntemperatures for the end of next week, but there is not a large \ncontingent of ensemble member on board for this at the moment.",
